    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="1284" n="1126" xml:id="pg1126"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    Thompson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with instruction No. 97, of
                    February 6 last, directing Mr. McCreery to make formal inquiry as to whether two
                    certain bonds issued by the Mexican Empire in 1864 are redeemable by the Mexican
                    treasury, I inclose herewith for your information a copy of a letter<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d234-f1"/> from Mr. G. T. Moeskes, inclosing a copy of
                    correspondence which he has had since then with the Mexican treasury on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
